The project was reconstructed in `/workspace` (no repo was checked out) to reproduce and fix the bug. The root cause: `config.Load()` read only the process environment, so a local `.env` was never consulted and `make run` panicked with `required environment variable DATABASE_URL is not set`.

**Fix 1 — add `github.com/joho/godotenv v1.5.1`:**

```
go get github.com/joho/godotenv@v1.5.1
```

**Fix 2 — load `.env` at the top of `config.Load()`, ignoring the error when `.env` is absent.** `godotenv.Load()` (not `Overload()`) never overrides variables already set in the process environment, so container `env_file` injection keeps working:

```go
package config

import (
	"fmt"
	"os"

	"github.com/joho/godotenv"
)

type Config struct {
	DatabaseURL string
	AppKey      []byte
}

// Load reads configuration from the environment, falling back to a local
// .env file when present, and panics if a required variable is still
// missing. godotenv.Load() never overrides variables already set in the
// process environment, so container env_file values always win; its error
// is ignored because a .env file is optional.
func Load() *Config {
	_ = godotenv.Load()

	dbURL := os.Getenv("DATABASE_URL")
	if dbURL == "" {
		panic("required environment variable DATABASE_URL is not set")
	}

	key := os.Getenv("APP_KEY")
	if len(key) != 32 {
		panic(fmt.Sprintf("required environment variable APP_KEY must be exactly 32 bytes, got %d", len(key)))
	}

	return &Config{DatabaseURL: dbURL, AppKey: []byte(key)}
}
```

**Fix 3 — `.env.example` placeholder** was 24 bytes (`0123456789abcdef01234567`) and tripped the 32-byte key validation once copied to `.env`; corrected to exactly 32 bytes:

```
APP_KEY=0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef
```

**Tests** (`internal/config/config_test.go`), including the two required ones:

```go
// TestLoad_EnvOverridesDotenv — .env has other values, process env wins (no-override).
func TestLoad_EnvOverridesDotenv(t *testing.T) {
	t.Setenv("DATABASE_URL", "postgres://env:secret@db:5432/env?sslmode=disable")
	t.Setenv("APP_KEY", envAppKey) // 32 bytes
	dir := t.TempDir()
	os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(dir, ".env"),
		[]byte("DATABASE_URL=postgres://dotenv:secret@db:5432/dotenv?sslmode=disable\n"+
			"APP_KEY=0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef\n"), 0o600)
	t.Chdir(dir)
	cfg := Load()
	// assert cfg.DatabaseURL == env value, cfg.AppKey == env value
}

// TestLoad_NoDotenvFile — empty dir, env vars set: Load succeeds.
func TestLoad_NoDotenvFile(t *testing.T) {
	t.Chdir(t.TempDir())
	t.Setenv("DATABASE_URL", "postgres://env:secret@db:5432/env?sslmode=disable")
	t.Setenv("APP_KEY", envAppKey)
	cfg := Load() // no panic, correct values
}
```

Plus edge-case tests: missing `DATABASE_URL` with no `.env` still panics (guard rail), and the 24-byte key is rejected while the 32-byte key is accepted.
